<article class="env-lemma" id="07JM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07JM">Lemma <span data-tag="07JM">60.18.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category endowed with the chaotic topology. Let $X$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$ such that every object of $\mathcal{C}$ has a morphism towards $X$. Assume that $\mathcal{C}$ has products of pairs. Then for every abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $\mathcal{C}$ the total cohomology $R\Gamma (\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{F})$ is represented by the complex </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F}(X) \to \mathcal{F}(X \times X) \to \mathcal{F}(X \times X \times X) \to \ldots  \]
</div>
  <p> associated to the cosimplicial abelian group $[n] \mapsto \mathcal{F}(X^ n)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $H^ q(X^ p, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for all $q > 0$ as any presheaf is a sheaf on $\mathcal{C}$. The assumption on $X$ is that $h_ X \to *$ is surjective. Using that $H^ q(X, \mathcal{F}) = H^ q(h_ X, \mathcal{F})$ and $H^ q(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{F}) = H^ q(*, \mathcal{F})$ we see that our statement is a special case of Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/079Z" data-tag="079Z">21.13.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>